#chap-header("3", "Races", "The Peoples of Ash")

The world of Ashen is a wild place. It is inhabited by magical and monstrous
creatures, shaped by technologies whose secrets of construction have long been
lost, and haunted by the legacy of gods who died at the end of the old world.
The Deathless who walk this land are themselves heirs to that legacy.

Race in Ashen describes what kind of body, senses, vulnerabilities, instincts,
and inherited powers a character has. It does not directly change your
attributes. Instead, it changes how your character interacts with the world:
what they can perceive, what harms them, how they recover, what kinds of magic
cling to them, and what physical assumptions apply when equipment, travel, or
survival matter.

Every player character is Deathless, but Deathlessness does not erase race. A
Clockwork returns as an immortal machine, an Echo returns as a remnant of dead
Faerie, a Human returns as one of the gods' divided firstborn, and a Soot-Beast
returns as a child of the Boar-Mother's warlike stock. These origins matter at
the table because they tie characters to factions, histories, prejudices,
patrons, enemies, and mysteries that can follow them across many deaths.

When choosing a race, read both the rules and the surrounding fiction. The
rules tell you what changes during play. The fiction tells you what assumptions
other people in the world may make about you, what memories might cling to your
old life, and what kinds of stories your character naturally invites.

The following entries present the playable peoples of Ashen and their subtypes.
Each entry gives a brief history, a physical and social overview, and the
special abilities that come from that origin.

